      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Look no further that RLE Group if you want a quality, professional installation.OK, that’s the summary, now for the details:After getting 3-4 random quotes (Facebook), I got onto SolarQuotes to get 3 proper quotes.  One never made contact, 2 did.  Ryan Looker from RLE Group made contact and came for a site visit.My requirements were: Lots of PV panels, 3 phase, wanting provision for a future battery.  Nearing retirement I wanted something that would reduce my power bills to nearly zero if possible.  I work from home now but will retire at the end of the year.Ryan suggested 45 Jinko PV panels and, initially, 2 Goodwe Inverters (one 10kW 3 phase & 1 5kW single phase).  In the end we went with one large SMA 15kW 3 phase.On the day of install Ryan and Will rocked up and the first thing they did was walk the roof inspecting the tiles.  Ours is a new build and only moved in the week before.  Ryan found 6 cracked/broken tiles.  I had spares and they replaced these after taking pictures of the bad tiles.   With bad weather, it was a bit hit-and-miss with getting the panels on the roof.  We have concrete tiles with a glaze and very slippery went wet.Install went very smoothly and very professionally, keeping us informed all the way on progress and any issues.  The only real issue was the rain and a small hick-up with SMA supplying the wrong MC4’s (?) – wrong mix of male/female I believe.  Ryan got on to SMA and all got sorted.As for the cabling? So neat and tidy, with no cables hanging down on the roof tiles.  Time spent doing the job right.  It is even pre-wired ready for a battery with a 250Amp disconnect in place, but not wired for safety reasons – but ready to go.All in all I couldn’t be happier with the workmanship, quality and professionalism.  It’s a cloudy rainy day as I write this and can see I’m still putting out 3.5Kw with ~13kWh today so far.Note that no gnomes were harmed during the installation and commissioning of this system.",
